content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-109 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-23500",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing-housing temperature is 85 °C. For this pump, bearing temperature is measured on the housing surface, with normal operation up to 70 °C, alarm at 80 °C and trip at 90 °C. Thus 85 °C is 15 °C above the normal limit and 5 °C above the alarm limit, but 5 °C below the trip limit: the alarm condition applies, not the trip condition. The above-alarm temperature also meets the maintenance procedure's high-temperature condition for bearing-pair replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The reported vibration is 2.5 mm/s. Figure 3's applicable limit is 2.8 mm/s RMS, the Zone A/Zone B boundary for velocity measured on bearing housings. If the report is an RMS bearing-housing reading, 2.5 mm/s falls in Zone A, 0.0–2.8 mm/s RMS ('New machines'), and is also below the 4.5 mm/s restricted-maintenance boundary and 7.1 mm/s damage-likely/stop boundary. This classification is provisional because the report does not state RMS, the measurement location, or the reading from the other housing; the highest reading from both housings must be classified.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No immediate-stop criterion is documented by the current readings: temperature is below the 90 °C trip, and the provisionally classified vibration is not in Zone D, 7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS, where damage is likely and the manual says to stop the pump. No leakage or noise is reported, but absence of noise does not remove the separate high-temperature bearing-replacement trigger.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing — investigate first because it is a documented probable cause of high bearing temperature; the current and specified grease quantities are not supplied, so this cause is not confirmed.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear — a documented probable cause of high bearing temperature. Inspect both bearings during the repair; lack of reported noise does not confirm that the bearings are serviceable.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment — another documented probable cause of high bearing temperature. Check alignment with a laser tool after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before disassembly, verify and record the drive-end bearing-housing surface temperature against the 70 °C normal, 80 °C alarm and 90 °C trip limits. Measure vibration velocity in mm/s RMS on both bearing housings, identify the highest reading, and classify it using Figure 3 rather than relying on the unqualified 2.5 mm/s report.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check and record the bearing grease quantity as part of the high-temperature troubleshooting. Do not assume a grease specification or quantity because none is provided in the evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before disassembly. Where removal of the back pull-out assembly is required, plan the lift for its documented 68 kg mass and use lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect both bearings and replace them as a pair, not only the drive-end bearing: install drive-end bearing HF3-512 (6312-C3) and non-drive-end bearing HF3-510 (6310-C3). The above-alarm housing-surface temperature is sufficient under section 5.3 to require pair replacement; investigate grease and alignment as possible underlying causes.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "During reassembly, use lightly oiled threads and tighten bearing-housing M12 bolts to 85 Nm. If other listed fasteners are disturbed, use the applicable Table 5 values: M16 casing bolts 210 Nm, M24 impeller nut 160 Nm and M10 seal-gland nuts 25 Nm. Install a new HF3-120 casing gasket if the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment. Acceptance tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before returning the pump to routine service, restore the documented Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry. Recheck housing-surface temperature and vibration on both bearing housings; compare temperature with the 70/80/90 °C limits and classify the highest vibration reading by its Figure 3 zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; replace together with the non-drive-end bearing because the high-temperature pair-replacement condition applies.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; replace together with the drive-end bearing because the high-temperature pair-replacement condition applies.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket, conditional on the casing being opened; the parts list requires replacement whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before pump disassembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly; do not plan a manual lift for that assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Apply the documented operating limits during verification and recommissioning: 90 °C is the bearing-housing temperature trip, and verified bearing-housing vibration in Zone D, 7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS, means damage is likely and the pump must be stopped.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement as a pair: standard time 6.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 12 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard time 1.5 hours with 1 technician, equivalent to 1.5 technician-hours; include this when the repair moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "There is an apparent scope difference within the same manual: the troubleshooting table says to replace bearings 'if worn' for high bearing temperature, while section 5.3, which that table references, requires both bearings to be replaced as a pair when either shows wear, noise or high temperature. Apply the more specific bearing-replacement procedure, section 5.3, to P-109: its 85 °C housing-surface measurement is above the 80 °C alarm and therefore triggers pair replacement even without reported noise. No competing manual revision, serial range or effective date is supplied to alter that decision.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Is the reported 2.5 mm/s an RMS vibration-velocity measurement on a bearing housing, which housing was measured, and what is the reading on the other housing? Figure 3 and the requirement to classify the highest of both housing readings cannot otherwise be applied conclusively [C06, C07].",
    "What are the specified bearing grease type and quantity, and how much grease is currently present? The troubleshooting table identifies over-greasing but supplies no grease specification [C09].",
    "What controlled step-by-step bearing-replacement procedure should be used, and does that procedure open the casing on this installation? The evidence gives the pair-replacement rule but not detailed bearing-removal steps; a new HF3-120 gasket is required if the casing is opened [C05, C10].",
    "Are there any later or serial-specific instructions for serial HF3-23500? Only document AQ-OM-300, Revision D, is supplied, with no serial applicability ranges or effective dates [C01].",
    "What site-specific isolation, lockout/tagout, PPE and permit requirements apply? These are not supplied; the evidence only documents pump isolation/draining and the lifting requirement [C02, C10].",
    "What additional labour should be allowed for preliminary measurements, grease checking and any conditional casing work? Table 6 provides standard times only for seal replacement, bearing-pair replacement and laser alignment [C12].",
    "The evidence does not define P1/P2/P3 response-time targets. Confirm the site response target; P2 has been selected as a planning decision because the temperature is above alarm but below trip, with no confirmed immediate-stop vibration condition [C02, C07]."
  ]
}
